  "method": "One drawing for six sizes. Vector outline scaled as U-185/190 (its 300 mm bottom slab then matches the printed 300); printed 300 mm slab and 300 mm (horizontal, vertical upper part) web kept. Sizes: top-flange zone (287 mm) fixed at the top, bottom zone (to the inner haunch, 375 mm) fixed, web region between stretched to H; webs and flanges translate with the top width A (soffit fixed). Two common factors fitted by least squares over all 12 A/I values: top-zone depth scale 0.86 and soffit half-width -85 mm. Per-size exact fits were rejected because they need implausible (0.2-0.35) top-flange scales for H165-H230.",
